IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. LOAN.
*> Monthly payment for a fixed-rate loan. A result that does not fit, or a
*> division by zero, gives status E and zero amounts instead of a bad number.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT IN-FILE  ASSIGN TO "INPUT.DAT"  ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.
    SELECT OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO "OUTPUT.DAT" ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD IN-FILE.
    COPY INREC.
FD OUT-FILE.
    COPY OUTREC.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-EOF  PIC X VALUE "N".
01 WS-R    PIC 9V9(10).
01 WS-PAY  PIC 9(7)V99.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-PARA.
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE OUTPUT OUT-FILE
    PERFORM UNTIL WS-EOF = "Y"
        READ IN-FILE
            AT END MOVE "Y" TO WS-EOF
            NOT AT END PERFORM PROCESS-PARA
        END-READ
    END-PERFORM
    CLOSE IN-FILE OUT-FILE
    STOP RUN.
PROCESS-PARA.
    MOVE IN-LOAN-ID TO OUT-LOAN-ID
    MOVE "K" TO OUT-STATUS
    MOVE 0 TO WS-PAY
    COMPUTE WS-R = IN-RATE / 12
    IF IN-RATE = 0
        COMPUTE WS-PAY ROUNDED = IN-PRINCIPAL / IN-TERM
            ON SIZE ERROR MOVE "E" TO OUT-STATUS
        END-COMPUTE
    ELSE
        COMPUTE WS-PAY ROUNDED =
            IN-PRINCIPAL * WS-R / (1 - (1 + WS-R) ** (0 - IN-TERM))
            ON SIZE ERROR MOVE "E" TO OUT-STATUS
        END-COMPUTE
    END-IF
    IF OUT-STATUS = "E"
        MOVE 0 TO OUT-PAYMENT
        MOVE 0 TO OUT-INTEREST
    ELSE
        MOVE WS-PAY TO OUT-PAYMENT
        COMPUTE OUT-INTEREST = WS-PAY * IN-TERM - IN-PRINCIPAL
    END-IF
    WRITE OUT-REC.
